 "meaning": "A triṣṭubh verse addressed to the priests: they are to bring their offering and their prayer to Agni, the bright and radiant, who knows and moves among all kinds of beings, divine and human. In the Taittirīya Brāhmaṇa (2.8.2) it is the yājyā for the omentum (vapā) of a victim offered to Agni, as Sāyaṇa states; it is also Ṛgveda 7.4.1. For Śukra (Venus) the tradition takes the verse because it begins with the word śukra, ‘bright’: that is all the words themselves show. The use of the verse for a graha belongs to the later gṛhya tradition, not to the Veda: in its source it serves another rite (see the commentary).",
 "in_the_rite": "The first mantra of Śukra’s step in the Navagraha sūktam, the graha’s own mantra in this tradition; the Saṃskāraratnamālā has śukraṃ te anyat instead (see the landing page).",
 "commentary": [
  {
   "who": "sayana",
   "label": "traditional",
   "text": "Sāyaṇa on TB 2.8.2: «अथ वपाया याज्यामाह»; «हे ऋत्विजः वो युष्माकमभीष्टसिद्ध्यर्थं शुक्राय निर्मलाय भानवे रश्मियुक्तायाग्नये सुपूतं सुष्ठु पूतं शुद्धमिदं हव्यं»; Agni «दैव्यानि देवविषयाणि मानुषा मनुष्यविषयाणि जनूंषि जन्मानि विद्मना वेदनेन जिगाति प्राप्नोति»."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
